{"title":"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Isosceles_trapezoid\" title=\"Isosceles trapezoid\">isosceles trapezoid</a> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/e/24e6207a6d63684aaef6a7eb34d386fbdb6979fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}||\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" /> whose angle at the longer base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/b/08bd824a65bb4b3ca2fcd409dd44f40dd046e61d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" />. The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Diagonal\" title=\"Diagonal\">diagonals</a> have length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/1/db13b53f07e035af23720aa7438fde64d491da8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\sqrt {21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />, and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is at distances <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/6/2369bfdb6daeb5c23b3b1eedc8c26eaddcc903e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\sqrt {7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab60cc06b90ee0dda17903c9e195d5038ce942f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\sqrt {7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"21\" /> from vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Altitude\" title=\"Altitude\">altitude</a> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />. The distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/4/2641cd10cfd314c37988fd8105e218c6527a7c5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\sqrt {n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bf1afcb274a3bb84338109fffec8a1f1c02008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/9091a509366e2723a7fb556a8255537bb23c13b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(300); defaultpen(1); pair A=(0,0), D=(4,0), B= A+2 expi(1/3*pi), C= D+2expi(2/3*pi), E=(-4/3,0), F=(3,0); draw(F--C--B--A); draw(E--A--D--C); draw(A--C,dashed); draw(circle(A,abs(C-A)),dotted); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,A,S); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,B,NW); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,D,SE); label(&quot;\\(E\\)&quot;,E,N); label(&quot;\\(F\\)&quot;,F,S); clip(currentpicture,(-1.5,-1)--(5,-1)--(5,3)--(-1.5,3)--cycle); [/asy]\" width=\"525\" height=\"365\" /></center>\n<p><b>Key observation.</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e4ebd5de591f3cf209353a8e6441a42f852c1dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 20\\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><b>Proof 1.</b> By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_inequality\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Triangle inequality\">triangle inequality</a>, we can immediately see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/e/48ef1ff3240a42f72d396cddaaad505472aec2eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD \\geq 20\\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"19\" />. However, notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87ecf07eb3776a3d44cce4cf9b134c77ebe91920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\sqrt{21} = 20\\sqrt{7}\\cdot\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"170\" height=\"33\" />, so by the law of sines, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e4ebd5de591f3cf209353a8e6441a42f852c1dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 20\\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55b591cd4cbc3cd3d8746972dae656279220ce9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACD$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is right and the circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/2/4f29958f511e3c88ce5d66d6e18bdd3d6de6804a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\sqrt{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />, which we will call <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> were increased, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> would have to be moved even farther outwards from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to maintain the angle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d2d0dc818ffa40c824ec87c9ad9c51fa86f458d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> could not touch it, a contradiction.\n</p><p><b>Proof 2.</b> Again, use the triangle inequality to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/e/48ef1ff3240a42f72d396cddaaad505472aec2eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD \\geq 20\\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"19\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/a/33ab3c8f2ad41073cfda7ce7e7305639821d3dd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = AD$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4fefe00fc71dd59b290161f8826a3ca9ab561a47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" />. By the law of cosines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8eabc87afe4c11a47e4aa27628d5517af4866b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/c/dacfbfa9871e40a6c4c685d0bd1beaf9905a9705.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2100 = x^2+y^2-xy \\iff y^2-xy+(x^2-2100) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"418\" height=\"19\" />. Viewing this as a quadratic in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, the discriminant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a737670d481129e2ead6d7223437f3cf70ea53f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> must satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/1596ce4be2bf6673b89e41886083daed4ae56c7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta = x^2-4(x^2-2100) = 8400-3x^2 \\geq 0 \\iff x \\leq 20\\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"453\" height=\"21\" />. Combining these two inequalities yields the desired conclusion.\n</p><p><br />\nThis observation tells us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear, in that order.\n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8eabc87afe4c11a47e4aa27628d5517af4866b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22bbdaf51a8a1faae81886d50358cbaf053ae08d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> triangles. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/a/0bacb065482a28530e953e66a019d187a901c843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF = 15\\sqrt {7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />, and\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/3/d23856decb7cf64df12003938a5fb775faab773e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF = EA + AF = 10\\sqrt {7} + 15\\sqrt {7} = 25\\sqrt {7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"329\" height=\"18\" />.</center>\n<p>Finally, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/f/c9fc1c67e78226499de0568a2a1f40f6acb83956.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25+7=\\boxed{032}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/e/81e7cd9b45373c3557d9c584c85b2919b46adfed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CAD$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Determine major angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9fe8455276bddfed734a1bc5315bcd085fa3c012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CAE$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e42fb9e0a718b0d73a24b2a5c431d30540a45225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><b>Lemma 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/e/aae8158db0246a8c274a3d4f9c50b7b42f9084e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACF = 90-\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"16\" /></b>\n</p><p>Angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e941e4bf1f3af58b5ecf459bc687b9c72f05d75f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CFA = 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" /> through altitude definition. Hence proved through complimentary angles.\n</p><p><b>Lemma 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/9/9d9e46e79b4c83de8a330eaa2ea5c139178b2b50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\theta&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" /></b>\n</p><p>Extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> to an arbitrary point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Then, angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/0/c401435802c19f2148bd2c29d9d90970dd2446d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACG = \\theta&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" />. Angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/4/b14dc39bb6c8f079bbeabc78c7443ec88974a211.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GCF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> is 90 degrees so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/0/8e0193f0d019de01a31e92abc19e668881f2fbc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACF = 90-\\theta&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"122\" height=\"17\" />. <b>Lemma 1</b> states <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/e/aae8158db0246a8c274a3d4f9c50b7b42f9084e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACF = 90-\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d12c7840ea7c841037d03076d277aff4815f194d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90-\\theta = 90-\\theta&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"17\" />, and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/9/9d9e46e79b4c83de8a330eaa2ea5c139178b2b50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\theta&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><b>2008 AIME I Q10:</b>\n</p><p>We quickly see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc2c7c43e46d222c619fb98cf8ee6357f8a65a58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta + \\theta&#39; = 2\\theta = 60, \\theta = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"19\" /> and angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/9495845e93e4d1eaa600108a431cbfb876152bbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADC = 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6ce2cd123db24a7b8373999aea7a98927e3b3c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> is a 30-60-90 triangle. It follows diagonal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dc145ba0904d4cbedf3d166c218016e267481f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\sqrt{21} = 10\\sqrt{7} \\cdot \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"157\" height=\"21\" /> is the leg of this triangle (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />) so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/1/4b17221cd4b611206f97d6b39e0924812ac93dd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = 10\\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"21\" />. This is furthermore supported from the fact <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/6/f0628c9ce7f518161fc54415384c6efc84fe9b77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = ED-EA = 20\\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"202\" height=\"21\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/6/0861a90144724d485d52181b420eccca560f7e50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FD = 5\\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/3/873efeff85fad87b43d52fbda166ac418ae56824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF = 30\\sqrt{7} - 5\\sqrt{7} = 25\\sqrt{7} \\implies \\boxed{032}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"307\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/238f77f5bd36cadced68f029e4554015289e50ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {AB}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, to meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/e/c4e6778bf0a1850f765de0f9458f3cb37a155c2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {DC}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> (extended through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />) at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35c11c783ddf150fb2c99ce6dd035d42bbaa7e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADG$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> is an equilateral triangle because of the angle conditions on the base.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50da584318afbd976721a144f2c7eae58bda9bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {GC} = x$\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/a/e4a54545e76d212230938524310aced8e219cb76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {CD} = 40\\sqrt{7}-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" />, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/5/3b5df2c499e5b2575bf9c1cb5d3dbabec7c54dc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{GD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/3/6834626125fde66c20977e4ca49a1b871d4b401f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 40\\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>By simple angle chasing, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/9/ad9b7c63ecfeea6fff934a7c02b93a4cf9671f9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CFD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is a 30-60-90 triangle and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b58ecdfe35e1049a10a184d9c08bfc416a70e796.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{FD} = \\frac{40\\sqrt{7}-x}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"131\" height=\"41\" />, \nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b83df036fa0c4b497331f16f1f28d5045cf4c6d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CF} = \\frac{40\\sqrt{21} - \\sqrt{3}x}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"163\" height=\"41\" /> \n</p><p>Similarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/4/e4430ae671256d44dd4f59655ecc9e7c5cc7eeb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CAF$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is a 30-60-90 triangle and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/d/dcd887df4ac56a6199e2f58c601eeea26e62c10a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CF} = \\frac{10\\sqrt{21}}{2} = 5\\sqrt{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"175\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Equating and solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a390704206da536749d6c269393ea8e32dfd1617.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 30\\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"21\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/423042653a6f5a6332604ed9ba83ae51226acb4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{FD} = \\frac{40\\sqrt{7}-x}{2} = 5\\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"191\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/1/c81ed257c59a0101443954944464ba0f639eb0b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{ED}-\\overline{FD} = \\overline{EF}$\" width=\"135\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/3/9e3635842881962f09ccdecb5ca452819db8a721.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\sqrt{7} - 5\\sqrt{7} = 25\\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"165\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/0/04047abe6fc5dd5082c38d178b4d5c1bfb295566.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 + 7 = \\boxed{032}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>How do you assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/3/6834626125fde66c20977e4ca49a1b871d4b401f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 40\\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>~polya_mouse.\n</p><p><br />\n(how is this a P10 what)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ciKy5RIgYjM?si=-aUCZCxRNqgXOKGz\">2008 AIME I #10</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://mathproblemsolvingskills.wordpress.com/\">MathProblemSolvingSkills.com</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I\" title=\"2008 AIME I\">2008 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2008\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017155351\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.055 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.078 seconds